flowchart LR
  accTitle: DorkOS replaceable interfaces
  accDescr: Each row names a caller, its port, and implementations. A port is a code boundary, not necessarily a network boundary. Dashed edges identify the unwired Buzz implementation and planned decision-model consumers; decision bridges themselves exist.
  ui["React client"] --> transport{{"Transport"}}
  transport --> http["HttpTransport<br/>HTTP + WebSocket + Space SSE<br/>Express"]
  dispatch["Session dispatcher"] --> agent{{"AgentRuntime"}}
  agent --> runtimes["Claude Code / Codex SDKs<br/>OpenCode HTTP + SSE sidecar<br/>Doe in-process engine"]
  accounts["Account actions"] --> connector{{"ConnectorProvider"}}
  connector --> backends["Composio · Nango · raw MCP<br/>Managed Cloud backend"]
  rooms["Local registry / remote consumers"] --> community{{"CommunityAdapter"}}
  community --> local["LocalCommunityAdapter<br/>Wraps local RoomService"]
  community --> remote["RemoteCommunityAdapter<br/>Owner-qualified, lazy instance<br/>Pinned server + space UUID<br/>Qualified HTTP + SSE"]
  community -.-> buzz["Buzz implementation<br/>Not wired"]
  notes["Agent memory"] --> memory{{"MemoryProvider"}}
  memory --> files["Built-in MEMORY.md store<br/>Optional registered backends"]
  relay["Relay message bus"] --> messaging{{"RelayAdapter"}}
  messaging --> channels["Messaging platforms / agent delivery<br/>Protocol depends on implementation"]
  future["Planned triage / moderation consumers"] -.->|"Not wired"| decision{{"DecisionModel"}}
  decision --> bridges["Rules · OpenAI-compatible · Jev<br/>Recommendation, not authority"]
  classDef port fill:#e7f1eb,stroke:#427a55,color:#183f26
  class transport,agent,connector,community,memory,messaging,decision port
